from pathlib import Path
import json, shutil, hashlib, html
ROOT=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[4]
HERE=Path(__file__).resolve().parent
RUN=ROOT/'ada_run/encounter_pilot/Random_Entropy/column-mixing'
for name in ['mixing-000','mixing-015','mixing-045','mixing-090','mixing-180','live-reading','columns-in-room']:
    shutil.copy2(RUN/(name+'.png'),HERE/(name+'.png'))
shutil.copy2(RUN/'report.json',HERE/'museum-report.json')
apparatus=json.loads((HERE/'verification.json').read_text(encoding='utf8'))
room=json.loads((HERE/'museum-report.json').read_text(encoding='utf8'))
assert apparatus['passed'] and room['passed']
counts=[len(apparatus['checks']),len(room['checks'])]
times=[0,15,45,90,180]
style='''*{box-sizing:border-box}body{margin:0;background:#edf0ed;color:#24343a;font:17px/1.55 system-ui,sans-serif}main{max-width:1550px;margin:auto;padding:22px}h1{margin:0;font:38px/1.2 Georgia,serif}h2{font:28px Georgia,serif}p{max-width:90ch}a{color:#286173}figure{margin:0}figure img{display:block;width:100%;max-height:70vh;object-fit:contain;background:#354454}figcaption{font-size:15px;padding:12px;background:#dce4e2}.timeline{border:0;margin:20px 0;padding:0}legend{margin-bottom:8px}input{accent-color:#356576;margin:0 4px 16px 12px}label{display:inline-block;padding:8px 14px;border:1px solid #9eafad;border-radius:5px;cursor:pointer}.frames figure{display:none}input:checked+label{background:#356576;color:white}.grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:22px;margin:32px 0}table{border-collapse:collapse}th,td{padding:8px 15px;border-bottom:1px solid #bbc6c5;text-align:right}th:first-child,td:first-child{text-align:left}nav{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:18px;margin:28px 0}pre{white-space:pre-wrap;font:16px/1.6 system-ui}summary{cursor:pointer}details{margin:24px 0}@media(max-width:750px){main{padding:15px}h1{font-size:30px}.grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}label{padding:5px 8px}input{margin-left:4px}th,td{padding:6px}}'''
style+=''.join(f'#t{t}:checked~.frames .s{t}{{display:block}}' for t in times)
captions={0:'Four starting arrangements, before mixing. Labels name these beginnings.',15:'15 seconds: red has crossed the layered column’s middle; the shell has dispersed sooner.',45:'45 seconds: all four are broadly mixed. Height readings in this retained run span 0.946–0.961 bits.',90:'90 seconds: the positions still differ. The original boundaries are much harder to recognise.',180:'180 seconds: mixing continues; local clusters and fluctuating readings remain. There is no final frozen image.'}
controls=''.join(f'<input type="radio" name="time" id="t{t}" {"checked" if t==0 else ""}><label for="t{t}">{"Start" if t==0 else str(t)+" seconds"}</label>' for t in times)
frames=''.join(f'<figure class="s{t}"><img src="mixing-{t:03d}.png" alt="{html.escape(captions[t])}" width="1600" height="1050"><figcaption>{html.escape(captions[t])}</figcaption></figure>' for t in times)
body=f'''<h1>When the beginnings become hard to see</h1><p>The four full-size columns now keep mixing. Forty red and forty blue beads remain in each; their starting arrangements gradually lose their visible separation.</p><fieldset class="timeline"><legend>Compare native room captures at the same viewpoint</legend>{controls}<div class="frames">{frames}</div></fieldset><p>These are saved frames from the actual Godot model, advanced to the stated times. The orthographic camera makes comparison easier; it is not a headset view or a human reading test.</p>
<section class="grid"><div><h2>In the room</h2><p>Approach to begin. Eight seconds leave the starting arrangements still, then all four mix continuously. PAUSE holds the current comparison. RESTART returns to the four beginnings and repeats their seeded paths.</p><p>The same bounded motion rule works in all four columns, with separate streams derived from 435. Nothing drives them towards a shared destination. Beads move through one another; this is a random-walk illustration, without fluid flow or a heat calculation.</p><p>Reload the museum and enter <strong>Entropy Workshop / Random_Entropy</strong>, after Entropy Types. The bank is near the entrance at (3,2).</p></div><figure><img src="live-reading.png" alt="The small side panel: two live readings, PAUSE and RESTART"><figcaption>Both readings follow the visible positions. The column’s overall colour count still gives one bit.</figcaption></figure></section>
<h2>What the trial shows</h2><p>By 45 seconds the four height readings are close. They fluctuate afterwards: local clusters can form while mixing continues. Similar numbers do not establish that the human eye sees no difference. That is the next observation to make.</p><table><caption>Height / core-rim colour uncertainty, bits</caption><thead><tr><th>Mixing time</th><th>A</th><th>B</th><th>C</th><th>D</th></tr></thead><tbody>'''
for sample in apparatus['samples']:
    body+=f'<tr><th>{sample["mixing_seconds"]:g} s</th>'+''.join(f'<td>{c["height_bits"]:.3f} / {c["radial_bits"]:.3f}</td>' for c in sample['columns'])+'</tr>'
body+=f'''</tbody></table><p>Human reading: keep the viewpoint fixed, watch without consulting the labels, then pause when a beginning becomes difficult to identify. Does another viewpoint or partition recover a difference? Record the observation, including no clear threshold.</p><p>{counts[0]} apparatus checks and {counts[1]} installed-room checks pass: starting records, conserved populations, containment, live measurements, frame-rate-independent paths, ongoing motion, restart, approach activation and pointer controls. Headset comfort and the perceptual comparison remain open.</p>'''
for name in ['final.md','tutorial.md']:
    text=(ROOT/'commons/maps/Random_Entropy'/name).read_text(encoding='utf8')
    (HERE/name).write_text(text,encoding='utf8')
    body+=f'<details><summary>Updated {name}</summary><pre>{html.escape(text)}</pre></details>'
body+='''<nav><a href="verification.json">Coordinates and apparatus checks</a><a href="museum-report.json">Room checks</a><a href="manifest.json">Source record</a><a href="../2026-10-16-entropy-columns/index.html">Previous still columns</a><a href="/long-museum/writing-wall?map=Random_Entropy">Writing wall</a></nav>'''
(HERE/'index.html').write_text('<!doctype html><html lang="en"><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Four beginnings, continuing mixing · Ada Research</title><style>'+style+'</style><main>'+body+'</main></html>',encoding='utf8')
files=[ROOT/'commons/artifacts/ordinary_entropies'/n for n in ['column_mixing.gd','jar_column.gd','jar_states.gd','jar_snapshot.gd']]+[ROOT/'commons/maps/Random_Entropy'/n for n in ['map_data.json','final.md','tutorial.md','plan.md','writing_wall.json']]
(HERE/'manifest.json').write_text(json.dumps({'checks':counts,'base_seed':435,'stream_seeds':[435+104729*i for i in range(4)],'hold_seconds':8,'step_seconds':0.12,'max_axis_step_metres':0.11,'mixing_sample_seconds':times,'no_claim':'Human perceptual equivalence or thermodynamic simulation','sha256':{p.relative_to(ROOT).as_posix():hashlib.sha256(p.read_bytes()).hexdigest() for p in files}},indent=2),encoding='utf8')
(HERE/'README.md').write_text('''# Four beginnings, continuing mixing

The user asks for the full-size columns to keep mixing until their visible differences fade. The new model preserves the previous starting coordinates and uses one colour-blind bounded random-walk rule with four distinct derived PRNG streams. Symmetric moves outside the usable cylinder are rejected; there is no clamping, common target or forced equality. Interpolation stays inside the convex boundary. Eight seconds on approach expose the starts. PAUSE/RESUME and RESTART occupy the existing side panel. Both measurements use the visible interpolated positions.

At 45 seconds the height readings in the native retained run span 0.946–0.961 bits. They fluctuate later. At 180 seconds one reaches 0.852: a finite record does not climb monotonically. Room images were inspected at 0 and 90 seconds, together with the live panel. The loss of recognisable starting boundaries is promising, but human perceptual identity is not verified. No physical headset trial was performed. Beads are point tracers with round glyphs: no bead collisions, heat or hydrodynamics.

Reproduce: `python -X utf8 doc/book/iterations/2026-10-16-column-mixing/run.py`, then `python -X utf8 tools/run_encounter_probe.py Random_Entropy --sequence randomness --render --no-bridges --output-tag column-mixing --probe doc/book/iterations/2026-10-16-column-mixing/museum_probe.gd`, then `publish.py`. Both native processes exited 0; no script/shader errors. Tests and coordinate records are in verification.json; installed-room checks are in museum-report.json. Static captures advance the actual model to explicit times, then hold it during rendering. Orthographic views are comparison tools, not headset screenshots.

Final, tutorial, catalog and planning notes follow the changed behavior. The hall order/placements, original hand-sized shakeable jar, prefab investigation and first 48-value research pilot remain unchanged.
''',encoding='utf8')
print('Published mixing comparison:',counts)
